analyses.1:
No trials yet. The starting net scores 0, and in past worlds that has usually meant the obs frame and the action/mask frame don't line up. Changing only the recipe or capacity has never moved a zero. Following the program, round 1 uses the reference net with the reference recipe (r about 0.95–1.25) and tests six hedge sets, all on one seed:
- the 4 layouts of set A;
- the 4 layouts of set B;
- A and B, each with the obs fed under all 8 grid symmetries (this targets obs/action reorientation, as in worlds 1 and 5);
- set A with per-cell LayerNorm on separate obs and mask stems and in the trunk, plus gain-0.01 outputs (this targets an unexpected input scale, as in world 4);
- set A with both obs symmetries and LayerNorm.
Any nonzero score tells us which deviation family this world has. In round 2 we split the best set into its 4 single layouts. Results are bimodal across seeds, so one zero is weak evidence. A 4-layout hedge typically scores 0.15–0.25.
